course: dictionary
lesson: 9251
title: A French word in English
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from other languages, and you can work out their meaning from the words around them. «Some signs look English but trick you: a librairie sells books, the hôtel de ville is the town hall, and sortie over a door means the way out.» The sentence tells you that sortie is a sign word, and a sign over a door shows the way out.
explain: Sortie is a French word, and it means going out. In a story about a castle under siege, the people inside may rush out to attack the enemy. That sudden attack is called a sortie.
explain: A sortie can also be one flight by a military aircraft on a mission, or a short, light-hearted trip out, like a sortie to the shops. Check each meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does it still make sense?
fact: Sortie is a noun, so you can have one sortie or many sorties.
fact: A sortie is a sudden attack made by soldiers rushing out from a place surrounded by enemies.
fact: A sortie is also one flight by a military aircraft on a mission.
fact: Informally, a sortie can be a short trip out somewhere, as in «a sortie to the shops».
fact: Sortie means exit in French, so on a door it means «the way out».
exercise: «The defenders made a sortie from the castle and caught the enemy by surprise.» What does sortie mean? | A quiet walk around the castle walls | A long war fought at sea | *A sudden attack from a place under siege | A type of medieval castle roof
exercise: On a door, the sign «sortie» means what? | Pull | Way in | *Way out | Push
exercise: Nadia says «a sortie to the shops» is a funny way of talking. In this humorous use, what does sortie mean? | The name of a shop | A soldier's sword | A flight by a jet | *A short trip out
test: «The pilot flew three sorties before lunch.» What does sortie mean here? | Sword fight | A cooking pot | *One flight on a military mission | A slow walk in the park
test: On the door signs, which word means «way in»? | tirez | sortie | *entrée | poussez
exam: The French word sortie means what in English? | Going home | Going up | *Going out | Coming in
